  {
    "key": "care-guide",
    "locale": "en-US",
    "path": "/guides/everyday-care",
    "published": true,
    "title": "A little care for every day",
    "type": "article",
    "summary": "Simple ways to build a comfortable daily routine for dogs and cats.",
    "body": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "The best routines leave room for your companion’s individual needs. Start with the basics, observe what they enjoy, and adjust as life changes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Make space for rest"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Offer a quiet, comfortable place to settle, with fresh water nearby. Keep bedding clean and check toys and accessories regularly for wear."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Make time for play"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Choose activities suited to your pet’s age, size and preferences. Supervise play and put away damaged toys. Cats may enjoy short, varied sessions; dogs often appreciate a mix of walks, play and downtime."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Notice the little things"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "children": [
          {
            "text": "Changes in appetite, behaviour or energy can be worth discussing with your veterinarian. For individual feeding, exercise and health advice, ask your veterinary team."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "imageKey": "home-companions"
  },
